# Real CRITICAL findings in the runtime image's Debian bookworm base
# packages, each with no available fix as of the date recorded below --
# confirmed by running `apt-get upgrade` in the image (deploy/docker/
# Dockerfile.app) and re-scanning: the installed version did not change,
# and Trivy's own `Status` column for each says why. This file accepts a
# real, currently-unfixable residual risk transparently (Constitution
# non-fabrication rule: the alternative -- silencing or lowering the scan's
# severity threshold -- would misrepresent "no fix exists yet" as "no
# vulnerability exists"). Re-run the container scan after any base-image
# bump; remove an entry once its `Fixed Version` is no longer empty.
#
# Recorded 2026-09-16 (Phase 18), python:3.11-slim-bookworm@sha256:528257d4...

# libsqlite3-0 3.40.1-2+deb12u2 -- Status: affected (no fixed version yet).
# Not reachable from this codebase: no service parses attacker-controlled
# SQLite files: Postgres is this repo's only relational store.
CVE-2025-7458

# perl-base 5.36.0-7+deb12u3 -- Status: affected. Perl is a Debian base-image
# transitive dependency (apt/dpkg tooling); this repository has no Perl
# code and never invokes an interpreter on untrusted input.
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-8376

# perl-base 5.36.0-7+deb12u3 -- Status: fix_deferred (Debian's own
# maintainers marked it not urgent enough to backport yet). Same
# unreachability rationale as above.
CVE-2026-42496

# zlib1g 1:1.2.13.dfsg-1 -- Status: will_not_fix (Debian will not patch this
# release). The affected path (zipOpenNewFileInZip4_6) is a ZIP-*writing*
# API; this codebase's own S3/object-store code only reads, and MinIO/S3
# operations here never shell out to zlib's CLI-adjacent write path.
CVE-2023-45853
